# Summary
Introduced: frontend-only control-plane auth unintentionally makes storage-node heartbeat authentication mandatory. The heartbeat path needs an independent storage-auth-required predicate, analogous to requires_frontend_runtime_map_auth, or the verifier should not be passed/enabled for storage heartbeats unless storage credentials are configured.
The new frontend runtime-map auth path builds a ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier even when no storage-node auth credentials are configured. The request dispatcher then treats the mere presence of any auth verifier as a requirement to authenticate RefreshNodeHeartbeat RPCs. As a result, a documented configuration that enables only ARGMIN_CONTROL_PLANE_FRONTEND_AUTH_CREDENTIALS, while leaving ARGMIN_CONTROL_PLANE_STORAGE_AUTH_CREDENTIALS unset, will reject otherwise-valid plain storage-node heartbeats. Storage nodes can lose leases and the cluster can become unavailable. This appears to be an introduced availability/configuration bug rather than a directly attacker-exploitable security vulnerability, because exploitation requires privileged control of server configuration.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm frontend-only configuration creates Some(ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier) with no storage-node credentials.
- [x] Confirm storage-node clients remain plain when storage auth credentials are unset.
- [x] Confirm RefreshNodeHeartbeat is gated only on auth_verifier.is_some(), unlike frontend runtime-map operations that use a frontend-specific predicate.
- [x] Dynamically prove a valid plain heartbeat is accepted without a verifier but rejected with a frontend-only verifier.
- [x] Capture debugger evidence that the frontend-only verifier causes dispatch into verify_storage_node_heartbeat_payload and envelope decoding of a plain heartbeat.
## Report
Validated the suspected bug. Key code evidence: crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:3145-3175 creates Some(ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier) whenever either storage or frontend credentials exist; with frontend-only credentials it uses ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier::new_empty(cluster_id), so storage_node_credentials is empty. crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:3267-3270 separately makes storage-node clients Plain when control_plane_storage_auth_credentials is empty. crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5452-5455 has a frontend-specific auth predicate, but crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:6208-6217 gates RefreshNodeHeartbeat only on auth_verifier being Some and unconditionally calls verify_storage_node_heartbeat_payload. That verifier decodes the payload as an auth envelope at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5580-5593 and records Missing when a plain heartbeat lacks auth magic.

Dynamic validation: I added a targeted unit-test PoC, poc_frontend_only_verifier_rejects_plain_storage_node_heartbeat, that constructs the same valid plain RefreshNodeHeartbeat twice. With auth_verifier=None it is accepted and grants lease deadline Some(2100). With a frontend-only verifier constructed via ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier::new_empty("auth-cluster").with_frontend_credentials(...), the same heartbeat is rejected before lease update. Reproduction command: cargo test -p storage --lib poc_frontend_only_verifier_rejects_plain_storage_node_heartbeat -- --nocapture. Output included: "frontend-only heartbeat rejection: control-plane RPC protocol error: control-plane auth envelope: invalid control-plane auth magic" and the test passed with 1 rejected StorageRuntimeMapRefresh/Missing metric.

I also ran the existing argmin-s3 test proving frontend-only configuration builds a verifier with zero storage credentials: cargo test -p argmin-s3 --bin argmin-s3 control_plane_unix_auth_verifier_includes_frontend_credentials -- --nocapture, which passed.

Crash/Valgrind/Debugger attempts: this is not a memory-safety crash; the direct PoC exits successfully while proving application-level rejection. valgrind and gdb were unavailable in the container. lldb was available and I ran the test binary with a breakpoint at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5580. The captured backtrace showed frame #0 ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier::verify_storage_node_heartbeat_payload at control_plane.rs:5580, called from frame #1 build_control_plane_unix_response_with_auth at control_plane.rs:6215, called from the PoC test at control_plane.rs:12432. This confirms the frontend-only verifier drives the plain heartbeat into the storage heartbeat auth verifier.

